From 566f3a6236943f8c562da84ae2ea6ad63cc5de3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:24:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: rewind to a turn, opened as a sub-thread
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.33 (ask 61; zed discussion #50192), with the
operator's choices of 2026-11-15: the rewound conversation opens as a
sub-thread and the original thread is kept as it was; the confirmation
asks every time whether the files go back too.

- acp_thread: AgentConnection gains supports_rewind_session and
  rewind_session(session, cut, restore_files) -> RewindOutcome {session_id,
  dropped_turns, files_restored}; the default refuses.
- agent_servers (v1): `_claude/rewind` {sessionId, at, restoreFiles}
  through send_task_request, offered when the agent advertises
  `_claude/rewind` (Claude Agent (Plus) 0.38.0). parse_rewind_answer reads
  plus's RewindResult strictly and turns every other status into words
  the user can act on; a conversation failure after the files were
  restored says the files were restored.
- agent_ui: beside 0112's fork button, a RotateCcw "Rewind to Here" on
  every finished turn but the last (has_later_turn: nothing after the last
  turn to rewind), root session only, disabled while a turn runs. The
  click (deferred past the view's update, as the fork's) asks "Rewind to
  this turn?" with Conversation Only / Conversation and Files / Cancel
  (rewind_choice), calls rewind_session with the turn's cut (turn_cut),
  and AgentPanel::open_rewound_sub_thread loads the answered session as a
  sub-thread linked to the parent (kind with_context, the kept turns'
  inherited count). A failure shows "Couldn't rewind: <reason>".
  sub_thread_request_at is shared by the fork and the rewind.

Known detail: the loaded sub-thread is titled "New Agent Thread" until
its first message, as the fork's is.

Tests: turn_fork::tests gains the confirmation's answers and "only a
turn with a later prompt can be rewound"; v1::rewind_tests (4) cover the
answer's statuses. Seen failing, each probe alone: rewind offered on
every turn (the later-prompt test), the files-restored warning dropped
(its test). Xvfb proof with a stub agent in the hub:
docs/assets/zeo-6.33-fork-from-turn-2026-11-15/ (the stub received
{"at": {"messageId": "msg_1"}, "restoreFiles": true} and the sub-thread
held the first turn only).
---

